# The Bishop's second job node: two angels for thirty seconds of a two-minute
# wait, one handing out damage and one dealing it.
#
# The Angel of Benevolence RE-GRANTS rather than standing -- GMS gives it a
# four-second buff every five seconds it is out, so the damage is up four
# seconds in five, and 20% of the wait rather than 25%. See Buff.duty_seconds;
# folding the duty into the numbers instead would have the card state 80%
# where GMS states 100%.
#
# The Avenging Angel's 4.02-second clock is published nowhere: every number in
# GMS's common block is spent by the readout, so the client holds this one. It
# is the community DPM calculator's measurement, the same source whose 3.03
# seconds Bahamut, Ifrit and Elquines already ship. Seven strikes a cast comes
# to 77,000%, or 642%/s of the wait -- well under Spirit of Snow's 1,715%/s,
# which is what a node carrying a buff this size should be.
#
# The mark is worth about a twentieth of a percent and is correct to have. It
# is spent by ONE LINE -- GMS's footnotes count the spend in hits -- so seven
# marks a cast buy seven lifted lines against the fourteen hundred a Bishop
# lands in the same two minutes. The angel cannot spend its own: GMS gives it
# no element, and only a holy hit spends one.
#
# The party's share keeps GMS's INT steps verbatim, as Benediction's do: 43,750
# INT reaches the 40% ceiling and a Bishop here tops out near 8,700, so the
# party is paid eleven points of it. Rescaling would state a different skill.
#
# Dropped: the MP, the attack reflection nothing here has, and "targets the
# boss with the highest HP first" -- a boss swing already takes the healthiest
# part standing. GMS's own "not usable while Bahamut is active" is dropped
# from the description too, being the older wording: the client dismisses the
# dragon instead, which is what silences_skill_name does and what the card's
# Dismisses row says.
name: "Angel of Balance"
description:
  "Summons an angel of compassion and vengeance. The Angel of Benevolence "
  "heals your party and increases your damage and theirs; the Avenging Angel "
  "strikes the enemy and marks what it hits."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BISHOP_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 120.0
mark {
  duration_seconds: 60.0
  final_dmg_pct: 0.10
  lifted_tag: SKILL_TAG_HOLY
}
buff {
  duration_seconds: 30.0
  duty_seconds: 4.0
  duty_interval_seconds: 5.0
  silences_skill_name: "Bahamut"
  base { damage_pct: 1.00 }
  ally_base {
    damage_pct: 0.05
    regen_pct: 0.102
    regen_interval_seconds: 5.0
  }
  ally_per_level { regen_pct: 0.002 }
  ally_int_lever {
    int_step: 1250
    effect { damage_pct: 0.01 }
    cap { damage_pct: 0.40 }
  }
  pulse {
    label: "Avenging Angel"
    cast_interval_seconds: 4.02
    lines: 10
    max_enemies: 12
    base { skill_pct: 5.20 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.20 }
  }
}
